  {
   "entry_id": "display-encoding",
   "subject": "Save Render 16-bit PNG under OCIO Default - sRGB (fixed pipeline)",
   "status": "calibrated",
   "formula": "code = round(65535 encode(binary16(clamp(L, 0, 1)))) per RGB channel, L the linear render, binary16 IEEE 754 half precision (round to nearest even), encode the IEC 61966-2-1 sRGB encoding. Empirical model of the observed codes: it states which codes an Iray render can contain, not how Iray computes them.",
   "public_sources": [
    {
     "source_id": "S-SRGB",
     "locator": "IEC 61966-2-1:1999 \u00a75.2 encoding"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "S-OCIO",
     "locator": "display/view transform of an OCIO project"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "S-EXR",
     "locator": "binary16 (half) pixel type"
    }
   ],
   "parameters": [
    {
     "name": "intermediate",
     "value": "binary16",
     "origin": "fitted"
    }
   ],
   "residuals": [],
   "notes": "44734063 of 46769247 interior RGB samples of the 66 fixture renders (0.9565) lie on the model's 10871-code lattice; every other sample is within 1 code of it."
  },
  {
   "entry_id": "environment-mapping",
   "subject": "Latitude-longitude environment orientation, lookup and intensity",
   "status": "calibrated",
   "formula": "Direction d (Y up) to texel: u = frac(atan2(-d.x, d.z) / (2 pi) + 1/4 + rotation / 360), v = acos(d.y) / pi (row 0 = +Y); bilinear on texel centres; radiance = file value x 2^exposure x s, exposure 0, s fitted once for all goldens. Orientation fitted on the mirror sphere (the eight sign/offset candidates differ by more than 13x in mean |delta|).",
   "public_sources": [
    {
     "source_id": "P-PBRT",
     "locator": "4th ed. \u00a712.5 image infinite lights"
